ADR-033 boundedness evidence: persistent EBUSY → Err in ≈ budget (800ms).

Verbatim capture (cargo test --bin tbard
providers::drm_backend::tests::test_retry_persistent_failure_is_bounded_by_budget
-- --nocapture):
  test providers::drm_backend::tests::test_retry_persistent_failure_is_bounded_by_budget ... ok
  test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 53 filtered
  out; finished in 0.80s

The test uses a 800ms budget + 50ms retry interval with a persistent
EBUSY closure. The boundedness assertion:
- `elapsed < budget + slack (1.5s)` — the wall-clock is bounded by the
  budget by construction.
- `elapsed >= budget - 150ms` — the retry ran for ~the budget, not bail
  early.
- The error is "Touch Bar DRM card never appeared: budget 800ms
  exhausted after N attempts" (NOT "aborted by shutdown").

The 30-min nested-retry case (NF-A1) is IMPOSSIBLE by construction:
there is no outer loop wrapping the retry. The wall-clock is bounded by
`budget` (800ms in the test; ~90s in production via
`DrmProvider::RETRY_BUDGET`).

The test serializes with the other shutdown-flag tests via
`SHUTDOWN_TEST_MUTEX` to prevent cross-test interference under the
parallel harness (a spurious shutdown from another test would make the
retry abort instead of exhausting the budget).